/**
Returns a promise that resolves when the limiter is idle.

The limiter is idle when there are no running or reserved slots and no functions waiting in the queue.

Calling this on an already idle limiter resolves normally. Multiple callers are supported and all resolve once the limiter becomes idle.

This is useful to know when all work submitted so far has settled.
*/
onIdle: () => Promise<void>;

### limit.pendingCount

The number of promises that are waiting to run (i.e. their internal `fn` was not called yet).

### limit.onIdle()

Returns a promise that resolves when the limiter is idle.

The limiter is idle when there are no running or reserved slots and no functions waiting in the queue.

Calling this on an already idle limiter resolves normally. Multiple callers are supported and all resolve once the limiter becomes idle.

This is useful to know when all work submitted so far has settled.

```js
import pLimit from 'p-limit';

const limit = pLimit(1);

limit(() => doSomething());
limit(() => doSomethingElse());

await limit.onIdle();
console.log('All work is done');
```

### limit.clearQueue()

